{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S111-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"6dba9f52e187f255522b71a27dd75d8fcf95e66ff70a4e0ec1c8d50900220ac0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 prepares for dismissal, but A5 prepares for mistakes rather than approaching rejection or loss.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 questions B2's promotion; A5 connects B4's responsibility to mistakes, though the box's purpose becomes obscure.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers promotion, but B4's 'More responsibility' supplies little managerial intention or pressure.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's box for mistakes weakens A1's concrete preparation for losing the job.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's meeting and packing box establish a playable employment conversation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's adaptable box is economical, but A5 makes its use metaphorical rather than playable.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 63\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You moved our meeting to Friday. I've brought a box for my desk.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's a promotion. You'll manage the new branch.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Away from everyone? I'll pack before they have to say goodbye.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You can still come to Friday drinks.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll bring my own glass. Better get used to being a visitor before they stop inviting me.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets changes and uncertainty as approaching loss and prepares before that loss arrives.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General pessimism can anticipate mistakes without treating a present cue as evidence of impending rejection.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 packs for dismissal; revised A3 treats relocation as separation and A5 extends protective packing to the team.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses an employer's helpful promotion to expand preparations; alternative b turns a partner's invitation into advance breakup logistics.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The rejected candidate's collective packing could be ordinary relocation assistance. The employment setting remains; B4 now offers continued social inclusion, which A5 treats as temporary access preceding exclusion. Internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, A1 prepares for dismissal and A5 rehearses becoming an outsider; logic 5, B2's branch causes A3's separation preparation and B4's drinks cause A5's visitor preparations; relationship 4, B2 advances A and B4 preserves contact; heightening 4, A5 anticipates eventual exclusion despite an invitation; specificity 5, A1 establishes a managerial meeting and desk box; brevity/wit 4, A5's own glass makes the feared status change tangible. Total 92. Unlike b's intimate breakup logistics, a prepares for losing workplace belonging.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's own glass is unnecessary at ordinary drinks; it must express A's sincere rehearsal of outsider status. The unchanged distinguishingEvidence describes the prior candidate's team packing, which this correction replaces. This is model review only.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S111-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"123cd97e1fbcb29b2cdf7b459b638f90c9c48a592b8ef96bcfc50970d4101340\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 treats a pause as goodbye and A3 converts swallowing tea into preparation for bad news.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's throat explanation, but A5 introduces an unexplained box after B4's dinner invitation.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 corrects the interpretation and B4 invites A, although their relationship remains indistinct.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns B4's invitation into a last dinner, but the new box distracts from that development.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a pause without establishing what question or relationship makes goodbye plausible.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's throat interpretation is concise; A5's box feels imported from the other alternative.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You paused when I asked about Saturday. Should I collect my things from your flat?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I was swallowing tea. I'm taking you to dinner.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Somewhere public. I'll bring tissues that fit in my sleeve.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's at home. I'm cooking your favourite.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll bring containers. You shouldn't have my leftovers haunting the fridge afterwards.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets pauses and changing plans as advance evidence of separation and organizes the aftermath.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking reassurance asks B to confirm acceptance; this card makes A prepare materially for expected loss.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 proposes bracing; revised A1 collects belongings and A5 prepares to remove leftovers after an imagined breakup.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a spreads anticipated workplace loss to colleagues; b makes affectionate domestic arrangements trigger increasingly intimate preparations.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision establishes a dating relationship and replaces the unexplained box with preparations caused by each invitation. Internal reread scores: 5, 5, 4, 4, 5, 4; total 92. B4 relocates dinner home, causing A5's fridge and container arrangements.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3 assumes the initial dinner is public; that inference is playable but depends on A's fearful interpretation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S112-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"228fe2223db4cf0e88f042bf25da308bff0916a82c89c2103311b1bfb4a7c7ab\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims authority over receiving news; A5 retains authority over timing even after B4 asserts capacity.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's ownership claim with workload; A5 explicitly redirects B4's 'handle' into timing.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 claims the letter and B4 claims emotional autonomy, forcing A to narrow the proposed control.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 restates timing authority already present in A1 rather than adding a concrete restriction.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's letter is playable, but A3's crowded day supplies no actual burden or relationship.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'timing of your handling it' explains the maneuver through abstract word repetition.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 79\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Give me the letter from the college. You've already had one disappointment today.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Mum, it's my application.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And if it's another rejection, I'll tell you after you've eaten.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can see 'Congratulations' through the window.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then after your brother's eaten. He didn't get in.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A assumes authority over what others learn and when they face it in order to manage their emotional burdens.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Practical support responds to someone's stated needs; this stance lets A decide whose feelings permit access to information.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 overrides B's declared capacity; revised A5 withholds good news to regulate an absent brother's disappointment.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses parental control of news; alternative b uses a sibling's protective management of incoming condolences.\",\n      \"reason\": \"A family college-admission setting replaces the unspecified letter. Internal reread scores: 5, 5, 4, 5, 5, 4; total 95. B4 removes the rejection rationale, causing A5 to extend emotional management to the brother.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The brother's rejection enters at A5; the reveal is coherent, but actors must establish A's protection as sincere.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S112-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"97dc56dff0fd5215b97336bb55899507482e6a3ee71c9360454430d6fd9ff6ce\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 takes difficult calls and A3 sorts emotional exposure, but A5 turns toward annoyance at B.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2 by filtering callers; A5 calls B4 an added objection without managing its emotional burden.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 needs direct contact, while B4 switches to a general statement about everyone's feelings.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes a retort about the list without increasing responsibility for anyone's feelings.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a difficult phone list but never identifies callers, occasion, or relationship.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's sorting is playable; A5's objections joke is less specific to emotional caretaking.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 63\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll take the condolence calls about Dad. You haven't slept.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I want to speak to Aunt June.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll check whether she's crying before I put her through.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She wants me to comfort her.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll comfort her first. You can have each other once I've got you both steady.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A takes charge of other people's emotional exposure and appoints themself the regulator of mutual support.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary helpfulness offers assistance; A instead decides when two relatives are emotionally eligible to speak.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 screens callers by upset; revised A5 makes both relatives' steadiness a condition of contact.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The letter alternative withholds information across a family; this alternative mediates two people's need to comfort each other.\",\n      \"reason\": \"A bereaved sibling setting supplies the missing relationships and turns B's information into expanded caretaking. Internal reread scores: 5, 5, 4, 4, 5, 4; total 92. B4 reveals June needs support, so A5 assumes responsibility for her too.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The scene has quiet controlling absurdity rather than a large joke; grief should remain an actual burden.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S113-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a0604f001690f36da94871882f4cd4cb7fc882c5443d5cb3707bb6b20ebf7836\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers adjustment for acceptance, A3 distrusts reassurance, and A5 seeks approval for complying.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 interprets B2's 'okay' as tired; A5 turns B4's request to stop changing into a distance check.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 reassures and B4 asks for stability, giving B a clear need that A struggles to satisfy.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes even stopping contingent on another reassurance, tightening the established loop.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's chair gives actors a physical issue, although the location and relationship are unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'right distance for stopping' grows economically from B4 and the chair established in A1.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 88\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Is my stool too close? I don't want you regretting our duet.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You're fine there. I need to see the music.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll move behind you. You won't have to look at me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Then I can't see you come in. Sit beside me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Beside you. Good. Could you nod before each entrance so I know you still want me joining in?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A repeatedly tests acceptance through B's responses and offers immediate self-adjustment when reassurance feels incomplete.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Fixating on one gesture preserves a single piece of evidence; A here reassesses each successive response.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 interprets B2's tone and A5 adapts to B4's new instruction, moving between cues rather than preserving one.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a negotiates physical proximity under B's frustration; revised b adjusts conversational behavior with an accepting new acquaintance.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The rejected original lacked an activity and gave the final check little consequence. A duet rehearsal is the new illustrative setting. Internal reread: fidelity 5, A3 treats B2's need to see music as personal rejection and A5 requests repeated acceptance; logic 5, B2 changes A3's seating and B4's need for visible entrances causes A5's nod request; relationship 4, B2 and B4 need a workable musical partnership; heightening 4, A5 makes each entrance require reassurance; specificity 5, A1 establishes shared music and seating; brevity/wit 4, A5 turns a useful musical cue into recurring permission to participate. Total 92. Alternative b tailors first-date conversation; a risks disrupting a joint performance.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The instrument is unspecified, so the seating must suit performers who can see each other and the music. The preserved distinguishingEvidence refers to the original tonal interpretation; this revision makes B2's practical qualification the incomplete reassurance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S113-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"6be5983cfb158ae67c4eebf38ee7507bd8aab5bba6a591874b72a5e2bcf8a686\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers to change the joke, A3 dissects 'fine,' and A5 seeks a more acceptable way to relax.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 directly tests B2's 'fine'; A5 directly incorporates B4's 'Relax' and the established joke.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 supply reassurance but reveal little personal want beyond calming A.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 asks another joke-related question without adding much consequence to A1's proposed adjustment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a joke's reception, but no occasion or relationship makes the concern particular.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'amused or ... tolerated' and A5's conditional relaxation are concise expressions of the stance.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 82\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"First dates don't need this many jokes. I'll stop.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I liked the one about your dog.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Just dog stories, then. I can do that.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'd like to hear about you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Absolutely. I'll start with who I was before the dog. Too far back?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns every response into a verdict on acceptance and immediately edits their behavior to secure a clearer yes.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Wanting praise for a joke concerns the joke's quality; A changes the kind of person they present to retain acceptance.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 asks how to relax acceptably; revised A3 restricts conversation to dogs and A5 immediately seeks approval for a new subject.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The chair alternative creates a loop around stopping physical adjustments; this first date uses B's interest to produce increasingly tailored self-presentation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision adds a first-date setting and gives B a positive desire to know A. Internal reread scores: 5, 5, 4, 4, 5, 4; total 92. B4 requests personal information, causing A5 to offer a biography while checking its acceptable scope.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The dog remains a conversational anchor rather than a described joke; inventing the joke is unnecessary for playing the exchange.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S114-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"32939ff990e2273ed78ca21464e9b7a9dd6082276b2592c97f64d552d45079f6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 reframes an empty opening as competence; A3 requests admiration and A5 relabels a hug as congratulations.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 replaces B2's sympathy with admiration; A5 accepts B4's hug only under the established endurance framing.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to sympathize and B4 offers physical comfort, prompting A to negotiate its meaning.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends A3's verbal demand for admiration to the meaning of an actual hug.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a failed opening with no audience, though its phrasing is conspicuously crafted.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's staying for the whole show earns A5's endurance framing; A1 is the wordiest turn.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You came to my solo show. Please stop saying 'brave' in that sad voice.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Three people walked out. I wanted to buy you a drink.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I finished anyway. You can buy a drink for that.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll invite the cast next door. They're celebrating a sellout.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. Tell them I finished with no audience at all. Let's see them do that.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes struggle proof of strength and permits concern only after converting its meaning into admiration.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Denying failure would erase the struggle; A acknowledges disaster and claims distinction for enduring it.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 calls the opening disastrous, while A3 cites staying and A5 accepts congratulations for endurance.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a negotiates the meaning of a friend's hug after public failure; b turns domestic care after physical exertion into a champion's reward.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The correction specifies A as a solo performer and replaces the repeated hug conversion with comparison to successful peers in an adjacent production. Internal reread: fidelity 5, A3 makes finishing merit a drink and A5 claims failure proves superior endurance; logic 4, B2's walkouts motivate A3 and B4's sellout supplies A5's comparison, although the final audience count is newly specified; relationship 4, B2 offers companionship and B4 includes fellow performers; heightening 5, A5 turns private consolation into a public claim of greater strength; specificity 5, A1 identifies the show and A's role; brevity/wit 4, A5's challenge follows the unequal audiences. Total 91. Alternative b conditions domestic care on a proud symbol; a seeks admiration from successful peers.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B's attendance and A5's empty audience require B to have left the auditorium before the finish; that remains unstated. The preserved distinguishingEvidence and alternativeComparison describe the original hug scene; the corrected evidence and comparison are recorded in reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S114-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"76f1ff0b7a42e5d166900362b22b24d95319648eb46c10fc961bd7b148885c71\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 rejects the poor-you face, A3 makes exhaustion impressive, and A5 requests a champion's framing.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 modifies B2's exhaustion diagnosis; A5 uses B4's tea offer to specify an admiring presentation.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 recognizes fatigue and B4 offers practical care, which A accepts under a condition.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves from correcting an adjective in A3 to directing how B delivers help.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a solo house move; B4's tea offer fits immediate recovery.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's two words enact the stance, while A5's mug request carries the same logic into a prop.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I carried the entire move myself. Please stop making that poor-you face.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You must be exhausted.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Impressively exhausted.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can I bring you tea?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. In the mug marked champion, not survivor.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recasts the visible cost of effort as an achievement and redirects help toward honoring that achievement.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Refusing assistance to prove independence would reject the tea; A accepts assistance when its symbolism affirms strength.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 acknowledges exhaustion and A5 says yes to B4's tea while controlling the mug's message.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The opening-night alternative seeks respect after failure; this move alternative seeks recognition for successfully carrying an excessive workload.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original passes and remains identical. Internal reread confirms scores 5, 5, 4, 4, 4, 4; total 90. B4's practical offer causes A5 to turn receiving care into receiving an award.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The marked mug is introduced at A5 and assumes a household where such a request is plausible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S115-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"094e482a36c845d5ebc7ed31c3553226f476651d39b54afc74b00c96a4db00f5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 prescribes a minute's silence for closure; A3 corrects posture and A5 prevents premature unplugging.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's dismissal with length of service; A5 makes B4's unplugging wait for the minute.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 questions the kettle's significance and B4 attempts a practical closing task.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 subjects the practical act of unplugging to the ceremony established at A1.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives a closing café, a kettle, and a specific ritual that can all be played immediately.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's seniority argument earns A5's 'final shift' without abandoning the farewell.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before we close the old café, one minute's silence for the kettle.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It was only a kettle.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It worked here longer than either of us. Stand properly.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can I unplug it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"After the minute. Don't interrupt its final shift.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A gives difficult farewell feelings a precise ceremony and corrects attempts to abbreviate or interrupt it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Sentimental attachment values the kettle; this card additionally regulates how and when others may say goodbye.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 specifies one minute, A3 corrects posture, and A5 makes unplugging conditional on completing the ritual.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a controls a workplace's final practical task through ceremony; revised b schedules shared family memories against a removal deadline.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original passes and remains identical. Internal reread confirms scores 5, 5, 4, 4, 5, 4; total 92. B4 proposes ending the kettle's service, causing A5 to protect the ceremony's timing.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The kettle personification is prominent; the café's closure must remain the emotional reason for the ritual.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S115-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"e8ad106d152a1e24d15f08e4445b86571c280ece64cc5af6fe6138c6e3401ad3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 imposes an order of remembrance and A3 blocks simplification, but the difficult feeling's cause is unstated.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 defers B2's story until after roses; A5 puts B4's shed story after the tree named in A1.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to tell a story and B4 identifies its subject, but no shared loss or practical pressure emerges.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats A3's queue enforcement with the next item rather than increasing its consequences.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies garden features without explaining why the garden is being remembered.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's tree having to finish is compact and follows A1's ordered remembrance.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 76\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before we hand over Mum's house keys, we say goodbye to her garden: roses, tree, shed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can I tell the story about her locking us in the shed?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"After the tree. She planted that first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The buyers are waiting outside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Bring them to the roses. If they're waiting for the keys, they can wait in the right order.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns the feelings of leaving into an ordered farewell and preserves that sequence when others introduce pressure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General procedural rigidity follows rules for their own sake; A's procedure organizes goodbye to a meaningful place.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 calls for remembrance; revised A1 explicitly ties the sequence to relinquishing Mum's house and A5 refuses to skip its emotional work.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The café scene delays unplugging until silence ends; this family scene responds to a deadline by recruiting additional participants into remembrance.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The house-handover setting remains. A5 no longer assumes buyers possess family memories or that more stories accelerate the ritual; their wait becomes subject to its sequence. Internal reread: fidelity 5, A1 orders goodbye and A5 extends that order to the handover; logic 4, B2's shed story is deferred by A3 and B4's buyers are brought into A5's queue; relationship 4, B2 wants remembrance while B4 needs to complete a transaction; heightening 4, A5 makes outsiders observe the family's sequence; specificity 5, A1's keys and B2's shed memory establish place and history; brevity/